<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Leros</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dodecanese-campaign">Dodecanese campaign</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Leros was fought in November 1943 on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> island of Leros, which British and Italian troops had held since <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> in September. After weeks of air attacks, German paratroopers and seaborne forces landed on 12 November and forced the garrison to surrender four days later. It was one of the last major German victories of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-leros.jpg" alt="Battle of Leros" width="320" height="502" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bauer · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_101I-527-2348-21,_Kreta,_Fallschirmj%C3%A4ger_vor_Start_mit_Ju_52.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
